{"duration_api_ms":153673,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"36642805-444a-4c58-9e21-37d94e0aacb1","total_cost_usd":1.2258848,"usage":{"input_tokens":42,"cache_creation_input_tokens":83605,"cache_read_input_tokens":1339984,"output_tokens":14444,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3392},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":83605,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":85196,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4389},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":42,"outputTokens":14444,"cacheReadInputTokens":1339984,"cacheCreationInputTokens":83605,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2258848,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3392,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NBCfsEJviqiof5tumQgJiJ","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-dotnet/tests/DcaShop.E2eTests && cat ShopUnderTest.cs BaseE2eTest.cs E2eFactAttribute.cs CheckoutGuestE2eTest.cs Pages/PaymentPage.cs Pages/ReviewPage.cs Pages/DeliveryPage.cs; git -C ../.. show --stat HEAD | head -30","description":"Read e2e infrastructure and checkout test"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011G3U6vY4AGy2uG7Hn8mV4j","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-dotnet && git show --stat HEAD | head -30","description":"Show the latest commit's files"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XrrDig4xAn8snpZyhXtaMQ","tool_input":{"command":"grep -n \"ToString\\|Format\\|Currency\" src/DcaShop.SharedKernel/Domain/Model/Money.cs | head; grep -rn \"order-summary-total\\|summary-total\" tests/DcaShop.E2eTests/Pages ../dca-ecommerce-sample-java/src/main/resources/templates 2>/dev/null | head","description":"Money formatting and existing total selectors"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UKRjpx4Ho2ueRERNqj3vSw","tool_input":{"command":"export PATH=$HOME/.dotnet:$PATH && dotnet build 2>&1 | tail -5 && dotnet test tests/DcaShop.E2eTests --logger trx --filter \"FullyQualifiedName~ProviderPaymentE2eTest\" 2>&1 | tail -25","timeout":600000,"description":"Build and run the new E2E test"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":30,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The test stage for `pay-through-the-provider` is finished, and the story gate for this stage passes. Each of the three criteria has one test, and each is red on its assertion, not on missing code.\n\n| criterion | test | level | fails on |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| authorized-payment-moves-to-review | `ProviderPaymentE2eTest#APaymentTheProviderAuthorizesLeadsOnToTheReview` | e2e (Playwright) | `Assert.Single`: the provider stub received no payment request |\n| refused-payment-stays-at-payment | `ProviderPaymentTest#ARefusedPaymentKeepsTheCustomerAtThePaymentStepWithTheRefusalText` | integration | the page redirects to the review (302) instead of staying on payment (200) |\n| slow-provider-counts-as-unavailable | `ProviderPaymentTest#AProviderThatAnswersOnlyAfterFiveSecondsCountsAsUnavailable` | integration | same assertion; it also requires an answer within 4 s |\n\nAn earlier run of this stage had already written the integration and unit tests. It left the browser test for the successful payment open until your answer to decision `pay-through-the-provider-01`. What I added this session:\n- **A payment-provider stub for the whole browser suite** (`tests/DcaShop.E2eTests/PaymentProviderStub.cs`). It starts with the shop, and `ShopUnderTest` gives the shop its address as `Checkout:PaymentProvider:BaseUrl`. By default it approves every payment, so the existing checkout browser tests will keep paying once the real provider replaces the in-sample stand-in. None of their lines changed, and they are green now.\n- **The browser test for the successful payment.** It reads the order total from the payment page and checks that the provider got exactly one payment request for that amount and currency. It runs alone, after the tests that run in parallel, so the requests the stub sees are only its own.\n- **Two page-object helpers:** `PaymentPage.TotalAsync()` and `ReviewPage.IsOnPage`.\n- **One markup attribute:** `data-test=\"order-summary-total\"` in `Views/Checkout/_OrderSummary.cshtml`, so the test can read the total. It changes no behaviour.\n\nTest runs:\n- **Unit:** 2 red, 176 green.\n- **Integration:** 6 red, 59 green.\n- **Browser:** 1 red, 37 green.\n\nEvery red test is one of this story's. `dotnet format` is clean.\n\nThree things need attention later:\n- **Shop started elsewhere:** if the suite is pointed at a shop via `E2E_BASE_URL`, that shop doesn't talk to the stub, so the new browser test fails there. That follows your decision that the suite starts its own shop.\n- **Java sample:** its order summary template needs the same `order-summary-total` attribute.\n- **Shared specification:** the new browser test's title needs a scenario in `scenarios.md`. That's yours to add.\n\nBoth sync items are noted in `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/tests.md` for the document stage. I ran no other stage and committed nothing.","ttft_ms":5497,"type":"result","duration_ms":269621,"uuid":"fc2c4a4f-67ad-4420-a476-3bfd1eece2bb","ttft_stream_ms":4341,"time_to_request_ms":55,"first_content_frame_ms":4341,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
